WEBVTT

1
00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:41.958
MY BELOVED DEMON

2
00:00:44.085 --> 00:00:46.921
<i>Protect us in battle.</i>

3
00:00:47.505 --> 00:00:49.799
<i>Be our protector</i>

4
00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:52.260
against evil and Satan's evil.

5
00:00:53.136 --> 00:00:56.222
Throw it in hell

6
00:00:56.306 --> 00:00:58.057
Satan and all evil spirits.

7
00:01:00.852 --> 00:01:02.979
<i>Trust in the Lord's mercy</i>

8
00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:06.816
and sincerely confess your sins. Amen.

9
00:01:09.194 --> 00:01:10.153
Amen.

10
00:01:14.699 --> 00:01:15.742
I…

11
00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:20.955
saw the devil

12
00:01:25.335 --> 00:01:26.920
Blinded by lust

13
00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:29.506
I didn't stop at anything

14
00:01:30.548 --> 00:01:32.675
as if possessed by the devil.

15
00:01:37.138 --> 00:01:39.224
And some tried to stop me.

16
00:01:41.976 --> 00:01:43.061
he said

17
00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:45.355
what will tell...

18
00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:50.151
about my misdeeds to the world.

19
00:01:52.654 --> 00:01:53.613
I assumed

20
00:01:54.531 --> 00:01:58.326
that he is trying to destroy me

21
00:01:59.327 --> 00:02:02.080
out of jealousy...

22
00:02:06.042 --> 00:02:12.590
EPISODE 13
PAST, ORIGINAL SIN

23
00:02:15.218 --> 00:02:16.719
{\an8}I really enjoyed the performance.

24
00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:23.852
{\an8}I finally understand
why are you so obsessed with tradition.

25
00:02:29.232 --> 00:02:31.151
{\an8}As for your human incarnation…

26
00:02:33.945 --> 00:02:34.821
{\an8}So Yi Sun.

27
00:02:36.531 --> 00:02:37.824
{\an8}That was my name.

28
00:02:41.911 --> 00:02:42.954
{\an8}So Yi Sun.

29
00:02:46.124 --> 00:02:47.333
{\an8}I like it.

30
00:02:48.626 --> 00:02:51.337
What happened to him in the end?

31
00:02:57.427 --> 00:02:59.178
<i>He killed himself.</i>

32
00:03:00.096 --> 00:03:01.347
<i>He did it,</i>

33
00:03:02.557 --> 00:03:04.058
<i>so as not to go to heaven.</i>

34
00:03:06.769 --> 00:03:08.897
He still didn't want to go there.

35
00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:10.565
And he didn't deserve it.

36
00:03:28.416 --> 00:03:31.127
I feel sorry for him.

37
00:03:40.178 --> 00:03:42.096
By the way, you obviously lied.

38
00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:45.183
You said their final
was neither happy nor sad

39
00:03:45.266 --> 00:03:47.352
that it was a simple and insignificant ending.

40
00:03:48.937 --> 00:03:50.063
This time

41
00:03:51.522 --> 00:03:53.024
I will choose the happy ending.

42
00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:13.253
Firefly?

43
00:04:13.962 --> 00:04:14.796
Yes.

44
00:04:57.255 --> 00:04:58.673
<i>Our reunion</i>

45
00:04:59.966 --> 00:05:01.467
<i>after such a long time</i>

46
00:05:03.052 --> 00:05:04.095
<i>could be</i>

47
00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:07.181
<i>my second chance.</i>

48
00:05:09.767 --> 00:05:10.893
<i>This time</i>

49
00:05:12.729 --> 00:05:14.689
<i>I will not make you unhappy under any circumstances.</i>

50
00:05:41.924 --> 00:05:43.426
Why are you here today?

51
00:05:45.136 --> 00:05:48.097
Sometimes I need peace and quiet.

52
00:05:48.723 --> 00:05:50.808
Does people-watching bring you peace?

53
00:05:50.892 --> 00:05:53.186
It can cause pain at the same time

54
00:05:53.269 --> 00:05:55.021
and calm down.

55
00:05:55.104 --> 00:05:57.106
Every coin has two sides.

56
00:05:58.316 --> 00:06:00.902
I don't want to repeat
unhappy past with To Hee.

57
00:06:01.944 --> 00:06:03.029
What should I do?

58
00:06:05.031 --> 00:06:06.532
Are you asking me for help?

59
00:06:06.616 --> 00:06:08.951
No, you won't help me anyway.

60
00:06:10.703 --> 00:06:11.746
I just…

61
00:06:13.414 --> 00:06:15.041
I ask your opinion.

62
00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:18.377
This would not be called misfortune,

63
00:06:18.461 --> 00:06:19.879
if it could be prevented.

64
00:06:22.048 --> 00:06:23.883
You really are no help.

65
00:06:23.966 --> 00:06:25.468
I thought my help was not needed.

66
00:06:28.137 --> 00:06:30.848
Happiness is meaningless without sorrow.

67
00:06:30.932 --> 00:06:33.976
People wouldn't appreciate happiness
if they had it all the time.

68
00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:36.896
You say it like grief
is of great value.

69
00:06:37.605 --> 00:06:39.315
But it is completely useless.

70
00:06:40.608 --> 00:06:42.527
People's lives are so short

71
00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:44.362
fortunately there are few of them.

72
00:06:53.204 --> 00:06:54.872
Sometimes happiness

73
00:06:55.623 --> 00:06:57.250
sometimes poisonous.

74
00:07:13.808 --> 00:07:15.810
Wake up To Hee.

75
00:07:18.563 --> 00:07:19.981
Five more minutes.

76
00:07:20.481 --> 00:07:22.942
Let's eat homemade food, as you wanted.

77
00:07:25.695 --> 00:07:26.654
Homemade food?

78
00:07:35.413 --> 00:07:38.916
So where is the homemade food?

79
00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:40.793
Close your eyes for a moment.

80
00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:43.337
Just for a moment.

81
00:07:57.643 --> 00:07:58.478
What is it?

82
00:08:00.104 --> 00:08:02.398
You remember I wanted home cooked food.

83
00:08:02.482 --> 00:08:03.524
Of course.

84
00:08:03.608 --> 00:08:05.109
I never forget your words.

85
00:08:06.235 --> 00:08:07.361
Male.

86
00:08:10.698 --> 00:08:11.657
It looks so good.

87
00:08:12.492 --> 00:08:13.534
- Shall we eat?
- Of course.

88
00:08:13.618 --> 00:08:15.995
But first, drink some water.

89
00:08:16.078 --> 00:08:17.914
hold on I'll go brush my teeth.

90
00:08:17.997 --> 00:08:20.166
I'll be back now. Don't start without me.

91
00:08:20.249 --> 00:08:21.459
Wait for me!

92
00:08:21.542 --> 00:08:23.044
But you can drink water!

93
00:08:32.762 --> 00:08:33.971
<i>It's already December.</i>

94
00:08:34.055 --> 00:08:35.515
Time flies.

95
00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:39.977
From a blind date to a wedding...

96
00:08:40.561 --> 00:08:42.230
It seems like a lifetime has passed.

97
00:08:43.314 --> 00:08:44.398
I know

98
00:08:44.482 --> 00:08:46.192
It was an eventful year.

99
00:08:48.069 --> 00:08:49.070
If you think about it,

100
00:08:49.153 --> 00:08:52.490
this will be our first Christmas together.

101
00:08:54.784 --> 00:08:57.495
But you don't like Christmas.

102
00:08:57.578 --> 00:08:58.412
This is not so.

103
00:08:58.496 --> 00:08:59.539
Now I love it.

104
00:08:59.622 --> 00:09:01.791
I like everything that you guys are up too.

105
00:09:01.874 --> 00:09:04.085
So I'm looking forward to our first Christmas.

106
00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:07.380
Then it's time to listen to some Christmas music.

107
00:09:20.268 --> 00:09:21.602
Why is the traffic so slow?

108
00:09:22.353 --> 00:09:23.771
There must have been an accident.

109
00:09:52.425 --> 00:09:53.259
To Hee

110
00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:55.595
What?

111
00:09:57.513 --> 00:09:59.265
What did we talk about?

112
00:10:01.851 --> 00:10:03.019
About Christmas.

113
00:10:03.936 --> 00:10:04.770
Yes.

114
00:10:05.396 --> 00:10:06.522
About Christmas.

115
00:10:08.858 --> 00:10:10.359
Let's listen to something else.

116
00:10:32.214 --> 00:10:33.591
Thank you.

117
00:10:44.226 --> 00:10:45.436
Drink.

118
00:10:45.519 --> 00:10:47.063
The perfect drink for this time of year.

119
00:10:55.655 --> 00:10:57.156
Great for waking me up.

120
00:10:59.325 --> 00:11:00.242
This is something new.

121
00:11:00.868 --> 00:11:02.995
I'm surprised you wanted to meet.

122
00:11:03.079 --> 00:11:06.624
It's because you know To Hee better than anyone.

123
00:11:07.208 --> 00:11:08.626
Did something happen to her?

124
00:11:09.210 --> 00:11:11.962
On the way to work, we saw an accident.

125
00:11:12.713 --> 00:11:13.756
<i>I think</i>

126
00:11:14.256 --> 00:11:16.884
<i>she reminded her of her parents' accident.</i>

127
00:11:19.804 --> 00:11:22.431
I want her to be happy all the time

128
00:11:22.932 --> 00:11:24.100
but she always seems to…

129
00:11:26.185 --> 00:11:27.895
feels guilty for her happiness.

130
00:11:27.978 --> 00:11:29.814
It could be wine

131
00:11:30.398 --> 00:11:31.649
or excitement

132
00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:33.317
She once said

133
00:11:34.443 --> 00:11:36.529
that several years
which she spent with her parents

134
00:11:36.612 --> 00:11:39.073
until their death

135
00:11:40.741 --> 00:11:43.327
<i>were the happiest period of her life.</i>

136
00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:49.917
Her life was full of grief at the top of happiness.

137
00:11:51.293 --> 00:11:54.964
Perhaps she is afraid of happiness.

138
00:11:55.464 --> 00:11:58.926
She moved
to Choo Jung Suk right after the accident?

139
00:11:59.009 --> 00:12:02.555
No, she lived with relatives for some time.

140
00:12:02.638 --> 00:12:05.975
Relatives gave her shelter
for her money and insurance

141
00:12:07.643 --> 00:12:11.439
but always left
the money was just running out.

142
00:12:13.774 --> 00:12:15.276
when i first met her

143
00:12:15.359 --> 00:12:18.279
she was like a porcupine.

144
00:12:19.572 --> 00:12:24.410
She treated everyone with deep distrust,
because she thought that they would leave her again.</i>

145
00:12:25.369 --> 00:12:27.788
<i>Aunt Jeon Suk opened To Hee's heart,</i>

146
00:12:29.039 --> 00:12:31.459
<i>but To Hee lost her too.</i>

147
00:12:33.043 --> 00:12:36.964
For a while To Hee
was looking for her killer.

148
00:12:38.799 --> 00:12:40.176
But the old wound...

149
00:12:41.886 --> 00:12:43.387
probably, it is given to her again.

150
00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:22.551
Come in.

151
00:13:23.177 --> 00:13:24.386
Meeting time.

152
00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:26.013
Good.

153
00:13:27.932 --> 00:13:29.767
<i>We are planning a promotional event,</i>

154
00:13:29.850 --> 00:13:32.394
to inform as best as possible

155
00:13:32.978 --> 00:13:35.272
about the new product "Mire Nutrition"

156
00:13:35.356 --> 00:13:38.400
and actively attract buyers.

157
00:13:38.484 --> 00:13:40.444
- Ms. Choi?
- Yes.

158
00:13:40.528 --> 00:13:42.321
As for the place

159
00:13:42.404 --> 00:13:46.075
we think of gyms, marathons,
university holidays, etc.

160
00:13:46.158 --> 00:13:47.117
Are there other options?

161
00:13:47.201 --> 00:13:48.953
These are all so obvious.

162
00:13:49.036 --> 00:13:50.913
I want a new and trendy place.

163
00:13:50.996 --> 00:13:52.665
How about

164
00:13:52.748 --> 00:13:53.999
"Sunwol Theater"?

165
00:13:54.583 --> 00:13:57.044
What does Director Jeon manage?

166
00:13:57.127 --> 00:13:59.255
Have you heard about the concept of "fashionable traditions"?

167
00:13:59.338 --> 00:14:01.507
Traditional culture is very popular now.

168
00:14:01.590 --> 00:14:04.843
And Ms. Chin's performance is on everyone's lips.

169
00:14:04.927 --> 00:14:07.221
I don't think this is a good idea.

170
00:14:07.304 --> 00:14:08.347
Who is Ms. Chin?

171
00:14:08.430 --> 00:14:10.182
She came here

172
00:14:10.266 --> 00:14:12.268
after a near fatal attack
to Mr. Chong.

173
00:14:12.768 --> 00:14:14.853
She even hugged him in front of everyone.

174
00:14:14.937 --> 00:14:16.272
you made a fuss

175
00:14:16.355 --> 00:14:18.649
they said it was more interesting
for Love and War, remember?

176
00:14:18.732 --> 00:14:20.859
What are you talking about? I didn't say that.

177
00:14:21.527 --> 00:14:22.528
Sorry.

178
00:14:22.611 --> 00:14:23.988
I like that thought.

179
00:14:25.781 --> 00:14:27.283
Let's cooperate with "Sunvol Theater".

180
00:14:29.869 --> 00:14:31.662
- Mrs. To.
- What?

181
00:14:34.206 --> 00:14:36.083
Ms. Sin will coordinate everything.

182
00:14:36.876 --> 00:14:37.960
Good.

183
00:14:38.586 --> 00:14:40.379
- Mrs. To.
- What?

184
00:14:48.762 --> 00:14:51.098
<i>Her life was full of grief at the top of happiness.</i>

185
00:14:51.599 --> 00:14:55.311
Perhaps she is afraid of happiness.

186
00:15:02.234 --> 00:15:03.944
- Ku Vone!
- Hello.

187
00:15:05.863 --> 00:15:07.656
You can hold a promotional event

188
00:15:07.740 --> 00:15:10.367
new product of my company
in "Sunvol Theater"?

189
00:15:10.451 --> 00:15:12.953
Whatever you want, To Hee.

190
00:15:13.537 --> 00:15:14.455
Don't say that.

191
00:15:14.538 --> 00:15:16.540
I am making a formal proposal,

192
00:15:16.624 --> 00:15:19.585
so please officially consider it
as executive director.

193
00:15:20.502 --> 00:15:22.087
Then I officially approve.

194
00:15:23.464 --> 00:15:24.298
Perfectly.

195
00:15:24.381 --> 00:15:27.468
So the marketing department of my company

196
00:15:27.551 --> 00:15:29.303
will send an offer.

197
00:15:30.429 --> 00:15:31.347
Here.

198
00:15:31.430 --> 00:15:32.848
- Look.
- Good.

199
00:15:32.932 --> 00:15:35.392
Let me explain quickly first.

200
00:15:35.476 --> 00:15:38.687
We will review the schedule of performances
and choose a date...

201
00:15:38.771 --> 00:15:40.105
<i>I'm worried.</i>

202
00:15:40.981 --> 00:15:42.858
<i>When the going gets tough,</i>

203
00:15:42.942 --> 00:15:45.194
<i>To Hee often works too hard.</i>

204
00:15:46.362 --> 00:15:49.156
<i>She suppresses emotions like that.</i>

205
00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:53.702
<i>Please stay with her,
to make sure,</i>

206
00:15:54.995 --> 00:15:56.747
<i>that she doesn't work too hard.</i>

207
00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:11.345
{\an8}MIRE GROUP CORPORATION

208
00:16:11.428 --> 00:16:12.471
{\an8}"MIRE FOUNDATION"

209
00:16:12.554 --> 00:16:14.556
{\an8}“Compensation Committee
in case of an accident at work"?

210
00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:18.769
{\an8}It was founded by Chairman Chu
and at that time it was unprecedented in Korea.

211
00:16:18.852 --> 00:16:22.773
This greatly improved the image of the company
after an accident at work,

212
00:16:22.856 --> 00:16:24.858
and therefore it is symbolically very valuable.

213
00:16:24.942 --> 00:16:26.694
Now it is obsolete.

214
00:16:27.861 --> 00:16:28.696
Let him go.

215
00:16:28.779 --> 00:16:31.865
Shareholders who believe
in Chairman Chu's management philosophy,

216
00:16:31.949 --> 00:16:33.409
will strongly resist.

217
00:16:33.492 --> 00:16:35.160
My mother is dead.

218
00:16:38.372 --> 00:16:40.541
As well as the world created by her.

219
00:16:42.167 --> 00:16:45.546
Let at least 30% of our employees
will switch to a part-time day.

220
00:16:45.629 --> 00:16:48.549
I want all subsidiaries
submitted restructuring plans.

221
00:16:53.595 --> 00:16:55.139
<i>You didn't live like that,</i>

222
00:16:55.222 --> 00:16:57.307
<i>as your father wanted.</i>

223
00:16:57.808 --> 00:16:59.184
That's why they punish you.

224
00:17:02.146 --> 00:17:04.106
Calm down!

225
00:17:08.610 --> 00:17:09.862
Now it's your turn.

226
00:18:30.442 --> 00:18:31.693
Mom?

227
00:18:32.361 --> 00:18:33.320
Daddy?

228
00:18:34.571 --> 00:18:36.281
where are you

229
00:18:37.324 --> 00:18:38.992
where did you go

230
00:18:45.207 --> 00:18:47.334
Where did you go without me?

231
00:19:09.106 --> 00:19:10.107
Daddy?

232
00:19:21.118 --> 00:19:22.578
Ku Vone?

233
00:19:28.083 --> 00:19:30.794
They all left without me.

234
00:19:31.587 --> 00:19:33.338
They left me here alone.

235
00:19:50.564 --> 00:19:52.274
It's all my fault.

236
00:19:54.526 --> 00:19:56.528
The responsibility lies with me.

237
00:20:03.577 --> 00:20:04.620
To Hee

238
00:20:05.913 --> 00:20:07.539
You didn't do anything wrong.

239
00:20:08.123 --> 00:20:09.166
Then…

240
00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:11.418
why did everyone leave

241
00:20:13.253 --> 00:20:15.130
Why did you leave me here alone?

242
00:20:16.006 --> 00:20:17.257
They did not leave you.

243
00:20:18.258 --> 00:20:19.301
Just…

244
00:20:21.136 --> 00:20:22.846
you won't be able to see them for a while.

245
00:20:23.513 --> 00:20:24.681
This means

246
00:20:24.765 --> 00:20:26.350
that I will see them again?

247
00:20:28.352 --> 00:20:29.394
Of course.

248
00:20:33.398 --> 00:20:34.900
Shall we go and see them now?

249
00:20:37.027 --> 00:20:37.945
Come on.

250
00:20:55.170 --> 00:20:56.922
Why is this one so big?

251
00:20:57.631 --> 00:20:59.299
Because she belongs at the top.

252
00:20:59.383 --> 00:21:00.634
Really?

253
00:21:04.596 --> 00:21:05.889
To Hee

254
00:21:05.973 --> 00:21:07.099
You are not sleeping.

255
00:21:09.476 --> 00:21:10.602
Mom

256
00:21:11.687 --> 00:21:12.854
Dad

257
00:21:12.938 --> 00:21:13.939
Hurry here.

258
00:21:14.022 --> 00:21:15.649
Won't you get gifts?

259
00:21:18.819 --> 00:21:20.195
Ms. Chu.

260
00:21:20.279 --> 00:21:22.364
we need you
to catch a star, To Hee.

261
00:21:22.447 --> 00:21:23.282
Come here.

262
00:21:30.622 --> 00:21:31.456
go

263
00:21:42.342 --> 00:21:43.552
Finally ready.

264
00:21:44.177 --> 00:21:46.471
Shall we eat cake now?

265
00:21:50.475 --> 00:21:51.560
Ku Vone.

266
00:22:50.118 --> 00:22:52.329
I wish I could actually return them to you.

267
00:22:54.831 --> 00:22:56.333
But this…

268
00:22:58.627 --> 00:22:59.920
all i can do

269
00:23:33.245 --> 00:23:35.705
Why can't I untangle this?

270
00:23:36.289 --> 00:23:39.167
Why the harder I try
then everything gets more confusing?

271
00:23:40.502 --> 00:23:41.419
What the…

272
00:23:43.130 --> 00:23:44.297
what are you doing

273
00:23:45.048 --> 00:23:46.174
You woke up.

274
00:23:47.425 --> 00:23:48.802
Christmas tree?

275
00:23:48.885 --> 00:23:49.719
Yes.

276
00:23:50.220 --> 00:23:51.805
But it's harder than it seems.

